# Repository-wide ignores.
#
# This is a two-component repository -- `proxy/` (the Java relay) and `hook/` (the native/managed
# in-process hook) -- so anything specific to one component lives in that component's own
# .gitignore: proxy/.gitignore and hook/.gitignore. What is left here is what applies to a checkout
# of the repository as a whole: editor state, OS droppings, and the compiler/linker artefacts that
# are not a source in any language.

### IntelliJ IDEA ###
out/
!**/src/main/**/out/
!**/src/test/**/out/
.kotlin
.idea/

### Eclipse ###
.apt_generated
.classpath
.factorypath
.project
.settings/
.springBeans
.sts4-cache
bin/
!**/src/main/**/bin/
!**/src/test/**/bin/

### NetBeans ###
/nbproject/private/
/nbbuild/
/dist/
/nbdist/
/.nb-gradle/

### VS Code ###
.vscode/

### Mac OS ###
.DS_Store

### Compiled output common to both components ###
*.class

# Linker and compiler program-database droppings, written beside whatever was built.
vc140.pdb
vc142.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib

### Python bytecode from the tooling in both components ###
__pycache__/
*.pyc

### Third-party binaries and archives (not ours to publish) ###
*.dll
*.exe
*.nupkg
*.zip

### Decompiled client source, wherever a tool decides to put it ###
/binaries/
/decomp/

### Subagent scratch directories ###
# Research agents download reference sources into a scratch directory. It is regenerable and never
# published; the distilled findings live under docs/.
/.research/
